  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN206.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">vāyil vēṇṭi ceṉṟa viṟalikkut talaimakaḷ vāyil maṟuttatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How SHE refused the door to the dancing girl who came in want of the door.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN206.1">
        <l>eṉṉeṉap paṭuṅko ṟōḻi naṉmakiḻp</l>
        <l>pēṭi peṇkoṇ ṭāṭukai kaṭuppa</l>
        <l>[na]kuvāyp paṭaitta tirimarup perumai</l>
        <l>mayirkaviṉ koṇṭa māttō lirumpuṟañ</l>
        <l>ciṟutoḻiṉ makāa rēṟic cēṇārkkun</l>
        <l>tuṟukaṉ mantiyiṟ ṟōṉṟu mūraṉ</l>
        <l>māri [yī]ṅkai māttaḷi raṉṉa</l>
        <l>vammā mēṉi yāyiḻai makaḷi</l>
        <l>rāran tāṅki[ya valarmulai] yākattu</l>
        <l>vārāk kātaloṭu tāriṭai kuḻaiya</l>
        <l>muḻavumukam pularā viḻa[vu]ṭai viyaṉakar</l>
        <l>vatuvai mēvala ṉākali ṉatupulattu</l>
        <l>vaṭupōr vēḷir [vī]rai muṉṟuṟai</l>
        <l>neṭuveḷ ḷuppi ṉirampāk kuppai</l>
        <l>perumpeyaṟ kuruki yāṅkut</l>
        <l>tiruntiḻai nekiḻntaṉa taṭameṉ ṟōḷē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1a-c 6d">What is to be said, friend? The man from a village,</l>
        <l corresp="2">where, while the dance of well intoxicated transvestites posing as women rages,</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c">the children with small tasks, mounting</l>
        <l corresp="4">the big backs with dark hide beautified by hair</l>
        <l corresp="3">of the buffaloes with twisted horns that form smiling mouths,</l>
        <l corresp="5d-6c">appear to all those who are at a distance like she-monkeys on thick stones,</l>
        <l corresp="10">because, while garlands turn to pulp from love[-making], coming in between</l>
        <l corresp="9">[his] chest [and] the blooming breasts that bear pearl necklaces</l>
        <l corresp="8">of women with choice jewels and bodies as pretty [and] dark</l>
        <l corresp="7">as the dark sprouts of the Mimosa in a shower,</l>
        <l corresp="11">in the wide town in a festival when the faces of the drums do not become dry,</l>
        <l corresp="12">he does not wish for marriage, in that field,</l>
        <l corresp="14">like long incomplete heaps of white salt,</l>
        <l corresp="13">on the front ghat of Vīrai, [belonging to] the Vēḷir of injurious battle,</l>
        <l corresp="15">melting because of great raining,</l>
        <l corresp="16">the broad soft shoulders of [her with] perfect jewels have become emaciated.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
